\begin{abstract}
We compare multinomial logistic regression (LR) with $k$-nearest neighbours
(\mbox{$k$-NN}, $k$ chosen by inner cross-validation) on Iris (OpenML 61) by
\NReps{} repetitions of stratified \NFolds-fold cross-validation (CV) on
identical splits. Accuracy is \LRAcc{} for LR (95\% interval \LRCI) and
\KNNAcc{} for $k$-NN (\KNNCI); the paired difference LR\,$-$\,$k$-NN is
\DiffAcc{} \DiffCI, \DiffVerdict: we detect no difference. Run once on the
Ibex cluster (node \texttt{\IbexNode}) and once locally, the CV
\IdentityVerdict.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction}
On Iris \citep{fisher1936} simple classifiers are so accurate that method
differences are small next to the variability of CV estimates. We ask whether
a linear (LR) and a local non-parametric ($k$-NN) classifier differ in
held-out accuracy, with intervals that respect the dependence between CV
folds, and whether the numbers reproduce across machines.

\section{Data and methods}
\paragraph{Data.} The code downloads Iris from OpenML \citep{vanschoren2014openml}
(dataset~61, version~\DataVersion, ARFF md5 checked against OpenML's):
\NSamples{} flowers, \NFeatures{} features, \NClasses{} classes of \NPerClass.
It is the UCI version with two known transcription errors
\citep{bezdek1999}, used as is.

\paragraph{Models.} Features are standardised inside each training set. LR is
multinomial (softmax), L2 penalty with $C=1$, L-BFGS, untuned. $k$-NN uses
Euclidean distance and uniform votes, with $k$ chosen from the odd values
\KMin--\KMax{} by stratified \NInner-fold CV on each outer training set only
(nested), ties to the smallest $k$. We use scikit-learn \SklearnVersion{}
\citep{pedregosa2011}.

\paragraph{Evaluation and intervals.} The outer protocol is \NReps{}
repetitions of stratified \NFolds-fold CV (seed \Seed): \NFoldsTotal{} splits
of \NTrain{} training and \NTest{} test flowers, the same for both methods, so
per-split differences are paired. Fold accuracies are dependent (training sets
overlap), so a naive $t$ interval is too narrow. For
each method and for the difference we use the corrected repeated-CV $t$
interval \citep{nadeau2003},
$\bar{x}\pm t_{0.975,\DF}\sqrt{(1/\NFoldsTotal+\NTest/\NTrain)\,s^2}$, with
$s^2$ the variance of the \NFoldsTotal{} fold values.

\paragraph{Reproducibility.} With single-threaded BLAS and pinned package
versions, the full CV ran once as a SLURM CPU job on the KAUST Ibex cluster
(job \IbexJob, node \texttt{\IbexNode}, \IbexCPU) and once locally
(\LocalCPU); we compare the two runs' per-fold outputs exactly.

